# ACF Fields

`Skaflow\Acf` (`lib/class-acf.php`) owns the integration. There is **no manual
PHP field registration** — every JSON file in `acf-json/` is loaded
automatically, and field groups appear wherever their location rules say.

## Creating a field group

Write `acf-json/group_{context}_{purpose}.json`. Naming follows
`group_{context}_{purpose}[_{specificity}]`, so groups sort into readable
families:

```
group_theme_options.json
group_product_additional_information.json
group_showroom_locations_term_fields.json
group_block_acf_field_display.json
```

Location rules decide where fields appear. For an ACF block:

```json
{
  "key": "group_your_block",
  "title": "Your Block",
  "fields": [
    { "key": "field_title", "label": "Title", "name": "title", "type": "text" }
  ],
  "location": [
    [ { "param": "block", "operator": "==", "value": "acf/your-block-name" } ]
  ]
}
```

Editing a group through the wp-admin UI re-exports the JSON automatically. Hand-
authored JSON is fine; keep `key` values unique.

## Options pages

A **Theme Options** page always exists, registered in `lib/class-acf.php` via
`acf_add_options_page()`. Its `menu_slug` is referenced by field group location
rules — changing the slug means updating every group that targets it.

Capability-specific configuration belongs on a sub-page under the relevant post
type, via `acf_add_options_sub_page()` with a `parent_slug`, rather than as
another tab on the global Theme Options page. Which sub-pages exist is
project-specific — see `PROJECT.md`.

Read option fields with the `'option'` post ID:

```php
$value = get_field( 'field_name', 'option' );
```

## The `render.php` context gotcha

Inside a block's `render.php`, a bare `get_field()` resolves against the
**block's** field group, not the post. To read a post field, pass the ID
explicitly:

```php
$block_field = get_field( 'block_setting' );              // block's own group
$post_field  = get_field( 'post_setting', get_the_ID() ); // the post
```

Use `get_block_wrapper_attributes()` for the block's wrapper attributes rather
than assembling a class string by hand.

## Guarding

ACF is a required plugin, but code should still degrade rather than fatal when a
function is missing:

```php
if ( ! function_exists( 'get_field' ) ) {
	return;
}
```

Never assume a field returns a value. Check before use, and provide a fallback
for anything rendered.

## Term and variation fields

Term fields work normally through a `taxonomy` location rule.

**Do not** use a `post_type == product_variation` location rule. That post type
has `show_ui: false`, so ACF has no screen to render on — variation fields need
native WooCommerce hooks instead. See `.cursor/rules/sf-commerce.mdc`.

## Debugging

```php
skaflow_write_log( get_fields() );
skaflow_dump( get_field( 'field_name' ) );
skaflow_write_log( acf_get_field_groups() );
```

When fields don't appear: check the location rules first, then that the group is
active, then that the field `name` matches the code exactly.

